{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932393-midnight-movies-horror-you-ve-seen-lately-and-its-potential-cofd-inspiration","id":932393,"title":"Midnight Movies: Horror you've seen lately, and its potential CofD inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-15T21:51:36-07:00","id":932393,"title":"Midnight Movies: Horror you've seen lately, and its potential CofD inspiration","content":"So, with this thread, I'm going to try to set up something I haven't seen before: a place for forum members to post a running tally of horror media they've consumed lately, and how it could be used as ChroD inspiration. That's what appeals to me most about the setting. I'm a ravenous, addicted horror buff, so ChroD gives me a chance to sort of put it all together- get creative and do stuff with themes and so on. <br /> <br /> So, I'll start:<br /> <br /> The most recent horror movie I watched was Southbound- which I watched specifically because a friend compared it to Midnight Roads (one of my all time favorite ChroD supplements of any line). It's really fantastic, and I especially love the &quot;angels&quot; that appear in it- the concept behind them, how they link the disparate stories, and the weird, twitchy, not-quite-real way they look and move. <br /> <br /> Bookwise, I'm rereading The Strain, which is a fantastic horror story in all aspects. Though it's about vampires and viral monsters, and works great if you need a jolt of inspiration for those, to me it's always been one of the works I associate the most with Hunter- at its heart, the book is about a disparate group of people who come together to fight a supernatural threat. You could also adapt its vampires as either a replacement for the Kindred or the Strix or another kind of Wicked Dead-style undead or a rare Bloodline or lost Clan. In universe, they're extremely virulent- anyone they feed on becomes a vampire- so their &quot;society&quot; is very strict about always killing anyone they feed from and controlling their population. That could be an interesting hook- Kindred dealing with an infestation of these strange vampires get an offer from the elders of the species to help them stamp out the outbreak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-16-2016, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T22:34:51-07:00","id":932411,"title":"","content":"I recommended a lot in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies\">Movies thread</a>. Though I tried to keep it neutral in terms of game lines as it was off-topic. I hadn't updated it much as interest seemed to wane but I'm a horror movie buff myself.<br /> <br /> The Invitation is very good for setting up mood and atmosphere. Technically it's a thriller, but you don't need supernatural elements to pack a thematic punch. It's also a great example of a blue book encounter, though I can't go into more without spoiling it.<br /> <br /> The Girl in the Photographs isn't a good movie but does depict an interesting slasher. Definitely ups the creepy vibe and there's a lot of little things you could pull from it to add tension.<br /> <br /> Holidays was just made available, and it's got a few very good ideas you could use. An anthology, some of the stories are very personal and would be hard to really get across outside of a one-on-one game, namely Father's Day, but the others contain characters and concepts that would fit in attached to a PC, with certain permissions, or NPC friends of the party. Mostly I'd suggest St. Patrick's Day, Easter or Mother's Day. Easy to imagine spirits or Gentry or darker things acting as influences behind the scenes there.<br /> <br /> Crush the Skull and the Collector are both really good, the former more of a dark comedy, the latter played more straight. They both depict protagonists going about a relatively simple task that, because of the darkness in the world, ends up being a lot more complicated. The Collector, in particular, was really good at depicting a game of cat and mouse where the cat doesn't know about the mouse and the mouse is trying to keep it that way. It would probably be a good test of Chronicle's quick crafting system.<br /> <br /> I found the Hallow to be one of the best depictions of changelings as scary that I've seen in a long time. Beyond the 'they're alien, they know not what they do' the things in it have a very malevolent edge to every aspect of them. And they really live up to their name and folklore. It really doesn't seem to fit Changeling the Lost, but you could probably make some hobgoblins out of it. If you didn't want to make them 'true' changelings there's more than enough things in the Chronicles of Darkness for them to emulate. I think they might be a better version of the fungus hosts, for instance, or an idigam trying to get in on the unseelie concept. It doesn't pull many punches, if you don't like the monsters and folklore, maybe it will inspire you to have an NPC jab a needle through the next time a PC looks through a hole.<br /> <br /> I'm basically just looking at recent Netflix stuff now, but the Stranger is a nice example of what happens <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">when a vampire comes to town and leaves a revenant in his wake. There's chaos. And while there aren't any vampire covenants in the movie, it's easy to imagine the All Night's Society running around trying to cover up the tracks of a massive Masquerade breach. For everyone else, well, chaos is just an invitation for PCs.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some Kind of Hate was, basically, a straight-up Geist the Sin-Eaters story, except the geist had a lot of independence and all the power. Lots of blood borne of a ghost out for vengeance riding the young man put in a similar position as her before her death.<br /> <br /> In terms of books, I've just finished Andre Duza's NoFace, which seems to read like an inspiration for Deviant, but really goes to show you how much fun and terror can be had with a simple Horror or two injected into the normal life of playing characters. The eponymous character and other Deviants are brutal and have interesting tactics that are bound to make encountering them interesting. Before that was Jack Kilborn's Endurance, which I suppose I could see for a one or two-session game but really offered more in the terms of a side story with something easily tied up with the God Machine, the VII or even Cheiron. It had some interesting characters, and certainly a lot one could use in a game, but as a book I think it left some to be desired. The same could be said about WEBCAM, by the same author, which is more of a slasher story played straight. The Slasher is interesting, in motive and modus operandi, but unless the characters were cops or very investigative hunters I couldn't see them getting involved with it easily, though it would be neat to see the Slasher targeting a galloi or something. Before that, because I was going on a Kilborn kick, was Afraid. Which was a very good book. It's sort of an invaders story, if the invaders were Deviants in the form of men. It would be so easy to really lure the players into it, but it requires them to be homebodies in a relatively small, or at least isolated, town. I'd really like to see supernaturals involved in it. Basically a 'red cell,' a group of controlled psychopaths, find their craft crashing in an American town and go about their objective, which is usually committing terrorism to strike fear into the heart of a populace so they won't fight back. Nicole Cushing's Mr. Suicide depicts a cult I've kept meaning to write up but I've never managed to get around to. Basically, to those for whom suicide is not enough, they offer Oblivion. Or at least, Oblivion might, if it 'likes' you. There's a series of trials one must go through, each further dehumanizing the adherent until they can reach that final step and be accepted, erased from reality as if they had never existed, the only evidence an 'artifact,' a random object of yours left behind with no real sense of how it got there.<br /> <br /> I was trying not to spoil too much but wonder if in the end I didn't give enough information, or gave too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-16-2016, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T22:43:02-07:00","id":932413,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.somethingawful.com/series/that-insidious-beast/\" target=\"_blank\">That Insidious Beast</a> is an obvious... something. Especially <i>Field Dominance</i>.<br /> <br /> Another good inspiration for a Mortals game would be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLdGl5mi0XeW0rOb8Ahw4L3kGflHJ9IdqF\" target=\"_blank\">Local 58</a>. I normally have no problem with horror, but these videos scare me <i>in broad daylight</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b><i>You Are On The Fastest Possible Route</i> (one of the Local 58 videos) is <i>great</i>, by the way. It reminded me of one of my favorite quotes from <i>A Society of Flowers</i>:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">The partnership did not prove fruitful;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">when we spent too long in their</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">company our counting numbers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">became suspect to ourselves.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 07-18-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T10:39:17-07:00","id":932558,"title":"","content":"I thought It Follows had the potential to make a really cool mortals game. I'd probably change the method by which it's transferred to another person, but the basic idea of the relentless horror that can find you anywhere, look like anyone, and can only be identified by the fact that no one else sees it is really cool, as is the idea of passing it on to someone else giving you a temporary reprieve until it kills them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T01:54:55-07:00","id":933321,"title":"","content":"<i>Stranger Things</i> is obviously a Hunter story, with one Deviant charachter. One of the characters looked like they were on the verge of becoming a Genius but it didn't go in that direction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-19-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T09:17:36-07:00","id":933446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932393-midnight-movies-horror-you-ve-seen-lately-and-its-potential-cofd-inspiration?p=933321#post933321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Stranger Things</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded, enthusiastically. I'm planning on using the electrokinetic Christmas light ouija board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 07-18-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name