after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:07:58-07:00","id":934045,"title":"","content":"Just finished John Langan's <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Fisherman-John-Langan-ebook/dp/B01FZSCUKO/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Fisherman</b></a>. Very fitting for blue books but can easily be associated into games for other supernaturals. At it's base is a protagonist whose friend is determined to go fishing with him in an isolated creek surrounded by rumors and warnings. As they discover more and more about the creek the friend's motive for wanting to go there is uncovered, as are many of its mysteries. There's some good examples of a story-within-a-story there, as well as the past coming back to lure folks of the future, and a little too much synchronicity, but it really goes a long way in depicting magic as a mysterious and dreadful thing, fitting for the more horror-bent games in Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-19-2016, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016